<title>SINGAPORE: Showpla to invest US$10.8 mln.</title>
<headline>Showpla to invest US$10.8 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plastic mouldings company Showpla Asia Ltd said on Wednesday it had pumped Singapore $15.3 million (US$10.8 million) into its investment arm Showpla International Pte Ltd (SIPL) to strengthen its operations in Vietnam, Thailand and Brazil.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement SIPL's share capital had been increased to S$19.3 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The capital injection is contributed jointly by Showpla Asia (60 percent) and the Government of Singapore Investment Corp (40 percent),&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Showpla makes injection moulded plastic components for consumer electronics industries.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
